Body:
I opened a PR for this: #13885

It implements a **template-based status line system** that resolves the core problem — zero-token display of session/project data in the TUI. Users define template strings in config, resolved server-side from built-in variables + shell commands + plugin-provided variables.

```jsonc
"tui": {
  "status_line": {
    "templates": {
      "terminal_title": "{project_name} ({shell:branch}) [{model_id}]",
      "session_footer": "{total_tokens:k} tok | ${total_cost} | ctx {context_used_pct:bar10} {context_used_pct}%",
      "home_footer": "{cwd:basename} on {shell:branch}"
    },
    "interval": 5,
    "commands": {
      "branch": "git branch --show-current",
      "dirty": "git diff-index --quiet HEAD -- 2>/dev/null && echo '' || echo '*'"
    }
  }
}
```

**Out of PR scope:**

The visual layout discussion that @Punchy25 and @davidsr2r raised — left/right alignment, multi-line bars, width-aware truncation, segmented rendering. The PR focuses on the **data layer**: what content is available and how to compose it into strings. The rendering is intentionally simple (single resolved string per target) so that layout decisions can be made separately without being coupled to the variable/template system.

This means a future layout PR could consume the same resolved templates and add segment splitting, alignment, or multi-line rendering on top — without changing the config schema or resolver.

